# Build context hygiene. Everything here is either a secret, a machine-local
# artifact, or bulk that would be sent to the daemon for no reason.

.git
.gitignore

# .env carries real credentials and must never enter an image -- an image is a
# distributable artifact and anything baked into a layer stays in that layer
# even if a later instruction deletes it. Config reaches the container as
# environment variables at run time instead.
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Leading **/ is load-bearing and its absence was a real defect: a bare `.env`
# pattern matches only the context ROOT, and the real file is api/.env, so a
# `COPY api/ ./` shipped live database credentials into an image layer. Verified
# by grepping the built image. Layers are immutable, so a later RM would not
# have removed it -- anyone who pulls the image can read the deleted file.
# .env.example is the CONTRACT, not a secret, and app/config.py refuses to start
# without it -- it is the file every key is validated against. Explicitly
# re-included after the wildcard above.
!**/.env.example

# Machine-local: this venv's scripts carry absolute paths to /Users/... and its
# wheels are macosx_11_0_arm64. Copying it into a linux/amd64 image would
# produce imports that fail at runtime rather than at build.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Evidence, notes and diagnosis write-ups. Useful to a reader, irrelevant to a
# running process, and some of it names tenant ids.
progress/
*.md

# Infrastructure definitions describe how to run containers; they do not belong
# inside one.
infra/
